program            = 003_computed_goto
area               = 08_gcc_extensions
description        = GCC computed goto through arrays of label addresses, folded constant index and volatile runtime index
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_audit_flags     = -Wall -Wextra -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror
ub_notes           <<END
UB-FREEDOM ARGUMENT. Every value is a small int; the largest computation is 10 * 3, far
from INT_MIN and INT_MAX, so there is no signed overflow. No shift operator is used. No
aliasing violation exists, since every object is accessed only through its own declared
type. Every object is initialized before it is read. No object is modified twice between
sequence points. Every printf call receives at most one side-effecting argument. Nothing
depends on padding bytes or on the addresses of unrelated objects.

Every index used in a goto * expression is provably in range: the folded chain uses the
literal indices 0, 1 and 2 into a three-element table; the runtime chain sets the
volatile index to exactly 0, then 1, then 2 into a three-element table; and the loop
dispatch selects 0 or 1 into a two-element table via a conditional expression that can
yield no other value. Each table is initialized with the address of a label that is
defined in the same function, so every jump target is valid.

Every path terminates. The folded chain is the straight line f_a to f_b to f_end. The
runtime chain is r_a to r_b to r_end. The loop is bounded: lp_i starts at 0 and is
incremented exactly once per pass, and the dispatch selects lp_exit as soon as lp_i
reaches 5, so it runs exactly five iterations. No label address is ever dereferenced as
data and none is printed.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
UB-GATE DEVIATION AND ITS REASON. Every program in area 08_gcc_extensions drops
-pedantic from the default warning gate. Reason: the constructs under test are
non-standard GCC extensions by definition, and -pedantic exists precisely to reject
them; retaining it would fail every program in the area for doing exactly what it is
meant to do. This is the only area-wide deviation in the corpus. No other warning is
relaxed: -Wall, -Wextra, -Wconversion, -Wsign-conversion, -Wshadow and -Werror are all
retained, and this program is clean under them, which is measured rather than asserted.

Nothing implementation-defined is observed, so no target restriction is needed and all
four targets are compared. The label-address arrays are declared static void *const
INSIDE main rather than at file scope, because &&label has no meaning outside the
function that owns the label and so cannot appear in a file-scope initializer. Placing
them in main also avoids the documented GCC hazard in which a static label-address array
inside an inlinable function can be initialized from a different clone's labels: main is
never inlined or cloned.

Label addresses are compared for distinctness only and the result is printed as the
boolean 1; no address or pointer value is ever printed, because addresses differ per
build and per target and would destroy byte-exact comparison. Comparing two label
addresses for inequality is well defined and target-independent.

Only int values are printed, so the measured width differences cannot be reached:
sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) are 4 on i686 and 8 on x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64.
No plain-char value the program computes is printed as a number or compared -- the only
plain-char objects are the format-string literals, copied through printf unchanged -- so
the measured char-signedness difference is not reached either: char is signed on x86_64
and i686 but unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64.

The runtime chain and the loop are indexed by volatile ints so that the optimizer cannot
resolve the dispatch statically and must emit a genuine indirect branch at -O1 and -O2,
while the folded chain uses literal indices the optimizer may lower to direct jumps. That
contrast is the point of the program: this is the two-variant rule applied to control
flow. The indirect-branch path is also the construct most likely to interact with the
indirect-branch hardening risk recorded as Partially mitigated in the project guide risk
register; that risk is the motivation for this program and is NOT an expected-divergence
basis, so this program carries no marker.

Output is identical on all four targets at all three optimization levels.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
cg_folded_acc=30
cg_folded_hits=2
cg_runtime_acc=30
cg_runtime_hits=2
cg_loop_sum=10
cg_loop_iters=5
cg_label_addrs_distinct=1
END
